Spain demands financial compensation for the enormous cost of the conflict.

Reluctantly, the United States agrees to pay an indemnity in exchange for the return of prisoners and a formal end to the war. Newspapers condemn the settlement as one of the greatest diplomatic humiliations in the nation's history, while Democratic politicians hold it up as proof of Republican incompetence.

The Treasury absorbs the financial burden, but the political cost may prove even greater.

- @End: Continue

@white_peace
subtitle: End the war without compensation.
